-    "zh": "活动的计数规律（whole-law-of-counting、counting-under-enclosure）读的是什么活跃；本结果读同一个展开中什么立着、什么依存。不被围住时，所立者与活跃者服从相同的计数规律：体现使两者相同，不纳入体现时两者都只受计数表约束。被围住时两者分开：流所取用与给予的是水平，所以平衡与耗散单独就为所立者定下变化界，体现所做的是把这个界从所立者带到活跃者。依存的计数不受前提约束，因为前提只在依存与活动、水平与世系一起时约束它：活动需要支持只要求活跃者所依存的支持它，有界传递只要求后代开始立着时所依存的，其亲代也依存，所需在一个界之内。读法（AI 论证）：被围住的展开所耗去的是立着的东西，活动只在体现时随之受约束；这是不用条件的理论中不加公理的计数规律在三个读法上的完整陈述，其中什么起约束（所纳入前提都起约束时）只对活动陈述。它不评价立起、不再立着、形成或消解。",
-    "en": "The laws of counting activity (whole-law-of-counting, counting-under-enclosure) read what is active; this result reads what stands and what depends in the same unfolding. Where nothing is enclosed what stands and what is active obey the same laws of counting: embodiment makes them one, and without it both are bound by the tally alone. Under enclosure they part: what the flow takes and gives is standing, so balance and dissipation alone bound the change of what stands, and what embodiment does is carry that bound from what stands to what is active. The counts of dependence are not bound by the premises, since the premises bear on dependence only together with activity, standing and descent: activity needing support asks only that what an active relatum depends on supports it, and bounded transmission only that what a descendant depends on as it comes to stand its parent depended on, within a bound. A reading (an AI argument): what an enclosed unfolding spends is what stands, activity being bound with it only where embodied; this completes the statement of the laws of counting of the theory without the condition, with no axiom, in the three readings, where binding (each chosen premise binding) is stated for activity only. It does not evaluate coming to stand, ceasing to stand, forming or dissolving."
